{
 "notes": ["The VS mode's KEEP SV (original scene 43: setup 0x0439a8 and 0x04373d, update 0x042f2d, drawn by 0x042b3a with the list 0x0426a4). The SYSTEM menu's KEEP SV opens it; it keeps copies of the hangars' Scoobees for the VS mode. The original keeps each as a file on the memory unit (0x06bc52 writes one, 0x06c057 reads the list, 0x06bf93 deletes one); the port keeps them in the settings file as vs_scoobees.", "Opening: the backdrop, the SV NAME and DATE labels and the HUD are there from the start; the frame grows from its centre over frame_seconds (16 frames), then the title and the arrows fade in over title_seconds (10 frames), then the slots grow from their centres one after another (slot_stagger apart, slot_grow_seconds each, from slots_from). Coming back from SV SPEC or the hangar skips it.", "The slots: seven cards slot_step apart from slot_first, clipped to clip; the first and last are the neighbours the scroll brings in. A card shows the kept Scoobee's body's maker (maker_cards, by maker), damaged for a Scoobee whose body is not in the tables, or empty for the rows past the end (drawn in the five visible slots only). The cursor's card is lit with the cursor frame over it, pulsing while the list takes input; the SV NAME and DATE show its Scoobee's name and when it was saved (the LOAD GAME digits).", "Up/down move between the list, SAVE and EXIT (sys 3); left/right move the cursor along the list (sys 19), the list scrolling by one slot over scroll_seconds when the cursor passes the fifth visible row. Cancel moves to EXIT (sys 3). The list always has at least five rows; confirm on an empty one buzzes (sys 8).", "A kept Scoobee's menu (popups.choose): SPEC opens SV SPEC on it, DELETE asks first (No chosen) and removes it, CANCEL goes back; a damaged one offers only DELETE and CANCEL. Left/right choose (sys 4), cancel moves to CANCEL (sys 4).", "SAVE offers MAKE when some hangar holds a complete Scoobee, or says there is none. MAKE opens the hangar from keep_sv (data/ui/hangar.json's origins): its KEEP comes back with that hangar's Scoobee, saved at once, or after asking (No chosen) when one of the same name is kept, where it takes that one's place.", "The cursor (the list's first row, the row and the column) is kept for coming back from SV SPEC and the hangar; from the SYSTEM menu it starts on SAVE. The original's memory unit notices (no room, failed to save or delete, damaged list, 0x042f2d states 10 to 15) have no counterpart on the PC and are not ported."],
